&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(102, 120, 140);&quot;&gt;We are always looking for amazing talent who can contribute to our growth and deliver results! Geotab is seeking a Solutions Engineer who will showcase and adapt Geotab solutions for partners and end-users by identifying customer needs, developing customized solutions, and supporting partners in overcoming their unique business challenges. This role plays a fundamental part in driving Geotab&#39;s strategies and advancing business objectives across sales channels, customer care, and product management. If you love technology and solving real-world problems for customers, and are keen to join an industry leader — we would love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(37, 71, 123);&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 120, 140); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As a Solutions Engineer, your key area of responsibility will be serving as a Subject Matter Expert on the Geotab ecosystem, empowering partners and end-users to maximize their use of Geotab&#39;s technology and so

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact at LILA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a talent-dense, high-agency AI safety team at Lila that will engage all core teams within the organization (science, model training, lab integration, etc.), to identify and mitigate risks from scientific superintelligence while retaining the core scientific discovery capabilities of the stack. The initial focus of this team will be to build and implement a bespoke safety strategy for Lila, tailored to its specific goals and deployment strategies. This will involve technical safety strategy development, broader ecosystem engagement, safety-focused evaluations, safety systems to mitigate risks, and a research agenda that explores longer-term needs such as oversight of superintelligent scientific systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As scientific AI systems become more capable and autonomous, their safety assessment and safeguards must develop alongside them. At Lila Sciences, you will help build the research methods and tools that make this possible, so that more and more decision-enablers can be automated safely. This will move us closer to the vision of a safety and security apparatus that is robust to a fully autonomous scientific engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your initial focus will be misuse: developing flexible and automated red-teaming approaches that test safety-relevant scientific capabilities and the robustness of safeguards. You will also contribute to safety automation beyond red teaming, helping the team evaluate, monitor and respond to risks across increasingly autonomous scientific workflows. You will own reusable research methods and assessment tools, working with mitigation engineers who implement protective mechanisms. We welcome Research Scientists and Research Engineers; responsibilities can span or evolve between the two profiles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run capability evaluations of scientific models, agents and tool-mediated workflows (including simulated lab environments), working with domain experts to make tests scientifically meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create methods or systems that explore diverse failure modes, adapt tests as evidence emerges and support systematic investigation beyond fixed benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reproducible experiments and evaluation tools that capture relevant behavior, outcomes and the evidence needed to interpret findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the quality and coverage of automated assessments, including failure cases in the evaluators themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop broader safety automation, across threat model management, evidence triage, regression testing, monitoring workflows or tools that help researchers assess and respond to risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with risk researchers and mitigation engineers to translate findings into improved assessments and safeguards, and verify whether those changes work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need to Succeed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong empirical judgment, practical programming ability and experience working with modern AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to investigate ambiguous failures, design informative comparisons and communicate limitations clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in scientific misuse risks and the ability to collaborate productively with domain specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For the Research Scientist profile:&lt;/strong&gt; evidence of selecting valuable research questions, developing or adapting methods, and designing experiments that yield defensible conclusions. You should be able to prototype and test your ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For the Research Engineer profile:&lt;/strong&gt; evidence of building reliable research software, evaluation infrastructure or agent systems that enabl

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You just graduated and you know you want a commercial career, but you&#39;re not sure which lane yet. Sales? Account management? Something else?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 months inside Flexport&#39;s commercial engine. Four rotations, four mentors, one goal: find where you fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Months 1–3: Open doors as an SDR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Months 4–6: Manage clients as an Account Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Months 7–9: Close deals alongside a top salesperson&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Months 10–12: Go deep in Operations, Marketing, or Customs — your pick&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have a named 1:1 mentor each block, plus one programme-wide buddy who stays with you the entire year. You&#39;ll also build with low-code tools alongside our engineering team. Global trade runs on tech now, not just relationships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The payoff: after a successful completion of the program you will get a permanent Account Executive, Business Development Rep, or Account Manager role by month 12, plus a company-wide network most new hires take years to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Block 1 – Sales Development: generate pipeline through outbound outreach, qualify leads, and keep Salesforce updated.&lt;br&gt;Block 2 – Account Management: support client meetings, identify upsell/renewal opportunities, and learn the customer lifecycle.&lt;br&gt;Block 3 – Sales: support a full sales cycle from discovery to close, including deal structuring and negotiation.&lt;br&gt;Block 4 – Elective: complete a project in Operations, Marketing, or Customs of your choice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside all four blocks, you&#39;ll also join Engineering sessions every two weeks, learn low-code/no-code tools, and build your own capstone project by year-end.&lt;/p&gt;
