&lt;h2&gt;Opportunity &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick Group is seeking an enthusiastic and analytical Apprentice BI Data Analyst to join its Group Business Intelligence (BI) team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group BI team plays a key role in supporting the business globally by delivering meaningful data, reporting and analysis to inform strategic decisions. Working closely with Finance, FP&amp;amp;A, the Commercial Hub and other business teams, the function develops and maintains reporting systems and BI dashboards, helping stakeholders better understand financial performance, revenue and recovery data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will work within the BI development team, reporting to the BI Technical Support Analyst. The role involves providing technical support, investigating and resolving reporting issues, and assisting with the development and improvement of dashboards to enhance self-service reporting across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside gaining hands-on experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365, Azure SQL Server and Power BI, the successful candidate will complete a Level 4 Data Analyst Apprenticeship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a motivated individual with strong analytical and interpersonal skills, a keen interest in data and technology, and a willingness to learn. Previous Business Intelligence experience is not required, as training and mentoring will be provided. Applicants must meet the apprenticeship eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day-to-day responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily integrity checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating issues raised by end-users and resolve them or escalating them to the development team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide immediate solutions to system issues and liaise with other support teams to ensure prompt resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage small scale changes through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality assurance tests and assisting with new release processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate and enhance workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer reporting security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with people across the firm to enable them to self-serve Business Intelligence through Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with developers to support the technical implementation and roll-out of new reporting dashboards on Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As skills and knowledge are gained, personally take on development work, through SQL and Power BI within the team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Brunswick, we seek smart and curious individuals dedicated to learning and growth. We value potential, strong work ethic, and excellent written and verbal communication skills. Standout candidates demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Excel, with an enthusiasm to develop more advanced skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in working with data and using it to solve business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate effectively with colleagues at all levels of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach and willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A resilient, enthusiastic team player with strong self-motivation and a collaborative, hands-on approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in databases and data; previous exposure to SQL would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in Business Intelligence and data visualisation; previous exposure to Power BI would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in developing commercial and financial understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of fun&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications close on &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Friday 30th October 2026 a

&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expose manufacturing defects in Graphcore’s advanced circuit boards with tests you build and deploy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Bristol, UK, you’ll develop board and PCBA hardware tests that help turn complex designs into reliable products. You’ll take tests from initial design analysis to deployment, then support them in factories and the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better defect coverage means more opportunities to identify manufacturing problems and understand hardware failures when products are in use. You’ll help make test and inspection methods work together, targeting the ways advanced electronic assemblies can go wrong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll examine PCB testability and susceptibility to manufacturing defects, then use that analysis to define and develop test solutions. You’ll build boundary scan and embedded functional tests, turning your understanding of board behaviour into practical diagnostic tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Test and Diagnosis team tackles hardware defects across chips, boards and finished systems. You’ll work directly with Hardware Design, Manufacturing Operations and contract electronics manufacturers, connecting design knowledge with factory experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use evidence to guide test decisions, challenge gaps in coverage and take responsibility for moving improvements forward. Move quickly from diagnosis to action, bringing the right people together to resolve hardware problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong electronics fundamentals, particularly digital electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial experience in board or PCBA hardware testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of manufacturing test for advanced electronic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of surface-mount technology (SMT), PCB manufacturing processes and their failure mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of automated optical inspection (AOI) and automated X-ray inspection (AXI) capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to diagnose electronic defects to component level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Electric Vehicle Scheme: Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa

